From d9cee50d3832b9d7d55b473e4054ccb76584e94c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:22:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notch-search: Search the system, not just apps

Besides apps the search from the notch now asks GNOME's search providers
(org.gnome.Shell.SearchProvider2) the way GNOME Shell does: settings,
contacts, calendar events, the calculator and whatever else has a key
file in gnome-shell/search-providers. GNOME Settings switches them on
and off and orders them (org.gnome.desktop.search-providers).

Each provider gets a section below the apps with up to three results.
A result opens in its app, the section's header opens the app with the
search. Results scroll above the keyboard.
